{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.AxialDistanceBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.AxialDistanceBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.two_le_natAbs_axialDist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.two_le_natAbs_axialDist","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AxialDistanceBound.lean#L61-L119","doc":"**An admissible swap has axial distance at least `2` in absolute value.**\n\nEquivalently: the scalar distances `±1` occur *exactly* in the same-row and same-column cases —\nthe converse of `axialDist_trichotomy`, which that theorem does not provide.\n\nThis is what keeps `offDiag` away from its zero: `offDiag q (-1) = 0`, so without this bound an\nadmissible swap could carry a vanishing off-diagonal entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.entry_lt_of_le_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.TableauCells.entry_lt_of_le_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/AxialDistanceBound.lean#L43-L59","doc":"**Entries increase strictly along the up-left order.**  Weakly up-left and not equal gives a\nstrict inequality, by one row step and one column step. ","signatureChunk":0}]}